<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑπερίων</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Hyperion,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>
			<i>the Sun-god</i>: he always joins <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ʽγ̔περίων Ἠέλιος</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.480
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.8
			</span></i>, al.), or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἠέλιος ʽ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υπερίων</span></span> (<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.133
			</span></i>), exc. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				369
			</span></i>, where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑπερίων</span> stands
			alone for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥλιος</span>; in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				31.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑπερίων</span> is father of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥλιος.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ʽγ̔περίων</span> (derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ ἰών</span>) is <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				58
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
